Ours (Music over RCS, 2026-10-30), applied to 186284e after gmessages-dedup-dm-txn.patch: the bridge handles only the
"message yourself" chat, the one-to-one chat with one of the phone's own numbers (the SIM numbers Google Messages gives
the bridge, the same test as the bot's ownChatRooms). Every other conversation is dropped as it arrives: its updates,
messages, typing and its entry in the conversation-list sync. GMESSAGES_ALL_CHATS=1 turns it off; a phone that hasn't
told the bridge any of its numbers keeps every chat. Test: pkg/connector/selfchat_test.go.

Why: the bridge made a room for every chat on the phone and copied every message into the homeserver, whose database
churn Litestream then uploaded to R2. On 2026-10-28 03:00-04:00 UTC that was about 75 MB of backups next to one 6.6 MB
song, and with it the service went over Render's 5 GB of monthly traffic on 2026-10-29. It also asked the phone about
chats nobody reads here (conversation details, contacts, media).

